course: dictionary
lesson: 7969
title: Reckless and risky words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words warn you about danger. Reckless is one of them. When you see it, look at the words around it to find out what is risky. «A reckless tackle, like sliding in studs up from behind, is a foul even if you touch the ball first.» The sentence tells you the tackle is dangerous and that the player did not care about hurting someone.
explain: Reckless means doing dangerous things without caring or thinking about what could go wrong. Read the words around it. Reckless driving, reckless behaviour and reckless with money all follow the same pattern: someone takes a risk and does not think about the harm it could cause.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try "A dangerous tackle, like sliding in studs up from behind, is a foul." It still makes sense, so dangerous is a good clue for reckless. Careful would not fit, so you know reckless is not about being careful.
fact: Reckless means doing dangerous things without caring or thinking about what could go wrong.
fact: Reckless can also describe something done in a careless, risky way, such as reckless spending.
fact: «A reckless tackle» is a dangerous tackle that puts the other player at risk.
fact: In everyday life, reckless behaviour, like running across a road without looking, can hurt you or others.
fact: Reckless is an adjective. Its forms are reckless, more reckless and most reckless.
exercise: «A reckless tackle, like sliding in studs up from behind, is a foul.» What does reckless mean? | Slow and careful | *Dangerous, without caring what could go wrong | Friendly and kind | Very tidy
exercise: Which example shows reckless behaviour? | Wearing a helmet when you ride your bike | Holding an adult's hand at the kerb | *Running across a busy road without looking | Looking both ways before you cross the road
exercise: Find and copy one word from «reckless driving» that tells you the driver is taking risks. | driving | the | *reckless | driver
test: Mia says, «He was reckless with his money and spent it all in one day.» What does reckless with money suggest? | Saving every penny carefully | *Spending without thinking about what could go wrong | Counting coins for hours | Giving money away to charity
test: Which word is closest in meaning to reckless? | *Careless | Gentle | Calm | Cautious
exam: Ben says, «The reckless rider raced through the red light.» Why is reckless a good word here? | It means the rider was slow and careful | It means the rider was lost | It means the light was broken | *It shows the rider took a dangerous risk without thinking
